d in the prompt does *not* have a `source_briefs` field in `paragraph_tasks`. It has `paragraph_id`, `point`, `development`, `source_uses`.\n    *Wait, let me re-read the instruction carefully:* \"引用负责人原任务，不重写研究内容：用 `source_briefs` 引用 `existing_paragraph_tasks` 的 `paragraph_id`；`point`/`development` 可省略，程序会回填负责人原文。你决定的是顺序、来源用途与衔接...\"\n    *But the Output Contract JSON schema says:*\n    ```json\n    \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"沿用输入中已有任务的 id，或用 <unit_id>_P<两位序号> 新建\",\n          \"point\": \"这一段要让读者得到的判断\",\n          \"development\": \"展开逻辑：先后顺序、比较维度、条件限定\",\n          \"source_uses\": [...]\n        }\n    ]\n    ```\n    *Conflict:* The instruction says \"point/development 可省略\" (can be omitted) if referencing existing tasks, but the schema implies they are fields. The instruction also says \"用 source_briefs 引用... paragraph_id\". The schema doesn't have `source_briefs`.\n    *Resolution:* I should follow the Output Contract JSON schema provided at the end of the prompt instructions, as that is the \"delivery contract\". However, the instruction about \"referencing existing tasks\" implies I should keep the `paragraph_id` from `existing_paragraph_tasks` and ideally keep the `point` and `development` consistent with them (or omit if the system fills them, but to be safe and clear for the writer, I should include them or ensure the ID matches so the system can merge). The instruction says \"每个已有段落 id 都必须被至少一个任务引用\".\n    *Actually, looking at the \"Paragraph Task Reference Contract\" section:* \"每个 paragraph_task 用 `source_briefs` 列出它来自哪些 `paragraph_id`... `point`/`development` 可以省略——程序会把负责人原文回填\".\n    *But the JSON Schema provided in \"输出合同\" does NOT have `source_briefs`.* It has `paragraph_id`.\n    *Decision:* I will use the `paragraph_id` from the input `existing_paragraph_tasks` for the `paragraph_id` field in the output. I will include `point` and `development` based on the input `existing_paragraph_tasks` to ensure clari